@startuml mms_release_happy
title MMS / Cloud Monolith — Weekly Release Train (Happy Path)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EAF4E9
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4C8C4A
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5

|Automated|
start

:**MONDAY — Release Kickoff**
(mms-release-kickoff-manual-deploy.yml)
confirm CLOUDP vYYYYMMDD fixVersion + QA plan
post announcement · DOCSP tickets · release_audit;

:**Slack poll posted** (#mms-developers)
proceed with branch cut? (informational — not a gate);
note right: Poll is informational only;\nrelease proceeds without explicit approval

:**BRANCH CUT** (PCT branch-cut engine)
cut from master -> vYYYYMMDD (weekly dated branch)
new Evergreen project mms-<version> (+ backports)
previous project set to LAMEDUCK
record candidate QA SHA;

:**QA** — set pointer mms-qa = SHA
deploy cloud-qa + cloud-qa-gov (all groups)
via Argo wt-mms-release;

:**Slack poll posted** (#mms-developers)
promote to staging? (informational — not a gate);
note right: Poll is informational only;\nrelease proceeds without explicit approval

:**STAGING** — set pointer mms-stage = SHA
deploy cloud-stage;

:**DEPLOY GATE** — PRE_PROD_DEPLOY_TESTS vs staging;
if (gate PASS?) then (yes)
  :push "deploy-gate pass" marker to prod S3 bucket
  mms-prod = SHA-green;
else (no)
  stop
endif

:**PROD GATE CHECK** (walk-back)
newest green staging SHA ahead of prod
decision = deploy;
note right
  dispatch mms-prod-deploy.yml
  NB: on THIS major train, prod is dispatched
  by the release flow itself. The weekday cron
  (mms-prod-deploy-trigger-cron.yml,
  cron '0 13 * * 1-5') is the **backport**
  mechanism and auto-skips during release week
  (skip-release-week when staging/prod branches
  differ). Cron is currently commented out
  (TODO cutover) — workflow_dispatch today.
  See mms-uml-diagram-backport.pu
end note

|Human|
:**PROD APPROVAL GATE**
mms-monolith-prod-deploy-approvers
(a human approves EVERY prod move);

|Automated|
partition "PROD" {
  fork
    :deploy group **dbs**;
  fork again
    :deploy group **resources**;
  end fork
  :deploy **web · backup(off) · billing** (WBB);
}
note right: via wt-deploy-mms-monolith-v2

|Human|
:approve-continue;

|Automated|
partition "PROD-GOV" {
  :deploy (+ wt-deploy-mms-alerts);
}
note right
  us-persons-prod gate
  ("US citizen on US soil")
  Mandated by **FedRAMP High**
  (approval mechanism could be improved)
end note

if (any PROD-GOV deploy FAILURES?) then (yes)
  |Human|
  :approve-continue
  (gate required only after prod-gov failures);
  |Automated|
else (no — no gate)
endif

partition "INTERNAL" {
  :deploy;
}

:**RELEASED**
SHA live on prod / prod-gov / internal
Jira vYYYYMMDD -> RELEASED;
stop

@enduml